#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114904 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/id #uuid "33326641-c2fa-53db-8ff5-8dedde2a16b1" :question/math-academy-id "e-3274" :question/problem "In square units, what is the area of $\\triangle ABC$ shown below?\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/ebf269e328b3f7a4ca08f735383c0865.png)" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal A = \\dfrac 1 2 AC \\cdot BC\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $\\angle B$, we have the length of the opposite side $\\overline{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overline{BC}$. Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan (m∠B) &= \\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\\n\\tan (60^{∘}) &= \\frac{9}{BC} \\\\\n\\sqrt{3} &= \\frac{9}{BC} \\\\\n\\sqrt{3}BC &= 9 \\\\\nBC &= \\frac{9}{\\sqrt{3}} \\\\\n&= \\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{3} \\\\\n&= 3\\sqrt{3}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 9 \\cdot (3\\sqrt{3}) \\\\\n&= \\frac{27\\sqrt{3}}{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114905 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio of One Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "60a0dba7-3007-5958-987a-d262091813cb" :question/math-academy-id "e-3277" :question/problem "Given that $\\tan(m\\angle{B}) =\\dfrac{4}{3}$, calculate the area (in square units) of $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/546392e4617aab57cfd9f51874ce6f0d.png)" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac12 BC \\cdot AC\n$$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\tan(m\\angle{B}) = \\dfrac{4}{3}\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to $\\angle{B}$, we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overline{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overline{BC}$. Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan (m∠B) &= \\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\\n\\frac{4}{3} &= \\frac{2x + 2}{2x} \\\\\n4 \\cdot 2x &= 3 \\cdot (2x + 2) \\\\\n8x &= 6x + 6 \\\\\n2x &= 6 \\\\\nx &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAC &= 2x + 2 = 2(3) + 2 = 8, \\\\\nBC &= 2x = 2(3) = 6\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2}BC \\cdot AC \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 6 \\cdot 8 \\\\\n&= 24\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114906 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given a Trigonometric Ratio of an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/id #uuid "514f238c-bac6-516a-a498-d1569db22471" :question/math-academy-id "e-3279" :question/problem "Given that $\\sin \\theta = \\dfrac 13$, calculate the area (in square units) of $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/33c414d6627752865e76dbefa5f35222.png)" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac12 AC \\cdot BC\n$$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\n\\sin \\theta = \\dfrac13\n$$\n\nwhere\n\n$$\n\\theta = m\\angle{A}\n$$\n\nNotice we're also given the length of the side $\\overline{BC}$ opposite to $\\angle{A}$. Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overline{AB}{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\sin θ &= \\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3} &= \\frac{5}{AB} \\\\\nAB &= 5(3) \\\\\nAB &= 15\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean theorem to find the missing side $AC$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nAC &= \\sqrt{AB^{2} - BC^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{15^{2} - 5^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{225 - 25} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{200} \\\\\n&= 10\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2}AC \\cdot BC \\\\\n&= \\frac{1}{2} \\cdot 10\\sqrt{2} \\cdot 5 \\\\\n&= 25\\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186114907 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given an Angle"}] :question/id #uuid "759db275-8647-5bf1-a3fb-dc014c920279" :question/math-academy-id "e-3282" :question/problem "In square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $\\triangle ABC$ shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/163510a23b9b562d8948b40bb29b7c12.png)" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\n\\mathcal{A} = \\dfrac12 AC \\cdot BC\n$$\n\nWe are given that\n\n$$\nm\\angle{B} = 23^\\circ\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to $\\angle{B}$, we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overline{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overline{BC}$. Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\tan (m∠B) &= \\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\\n\\tan (23^{∘}) &= \\frac{x - 1}{2x} \\\\\n2x \\cdot \\tan (23^{∘}) &= x - 1 \\\\\n1 &= x - 2x \\cdot \\tan (23^{∘}) \\\\\n1 &= x(1 - 2 \\cdot \\tan (23^{∘})) \\\\\nx &= (1)/(1 - 2 \\cdot \\tan (23^{∘})) \\\\\nx &= 6.6203…\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nBC &= 2x = 2(6.6203…) = 13.2406…, \\\\\nAC &= x - 1 = (6.6203…) - 1 = 5.6203…\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $\\triangle{ABC}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nA &= \\frac{1}{2}(5.6203…)(13.2406…) \\\\\n&= 37.2080… \\\\\n&\\approx 37.2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252558 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given a Trigonometric Ratio of an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d7a25d3d-74ea-56ed-8931-14f46984d29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252560} {:answer/id #uuid "12e72070-ddac-5240-a4f3-e64f07645843" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "180" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252561} {:answer/id #uuid "e3c3a4f1-4bd3-5fdb-9510-756ad4769b5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "210" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252562} {:answer/id #uuid "01c1ef96-e707-5873-9dc2-04854dcb41ab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "150" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252563} {:answer/id #uuid "f0b35384-c99a-56ac-b1f5-ea1ceabfec87" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "240" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252564}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d7a25d3d-74ea-56ed-8931-14f46984d29a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "270" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252560} :answer-field/id #uuid "0e9da70e-743e-522d-b545-2ea535a8382b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252559}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "ee965f67-bb44-5997-ae93-829735f50901" :question/math-academy-id "q-124466" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/4784e18b0e3631272efa1c002e686e9349ea04a900d8bc1e6b0416c09e994ccb.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =\\frac{5}{3},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AB}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3} & =\\frac{AC}{18} \\\\ \\frac{5}{3}\\cdot 18 & =AC \\\\ AC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 18 \\\\  & =270.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252565 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63eedc9b-db3e-581b-9940-2913e71e796e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252567} {:answer/id #uuid "7cf34dda-628b-57bd-b350-78befeae4976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252568} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b6bea3-e9d9-50e5-a9b6-27e8f753a19f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "40" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252569} {:answer/id #uuid "3e01d1a2-1c50-52e1-a59b-0070bde853a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "36" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252570} {:answer/id #uuid "dc38716b-0b31-5603-a6cc-89db61be99fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252571}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7cf34dda-628b-57bd-b350-78befeae4976" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252568} :answer-field/id #uuid "f0745145-08f0-5e22-ba56-c5b6e3447a31" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252566}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c661f073-d3a4-584b-af91-436e2a5fe0cc" :question/math-academy-id "q-124470" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/5c7116b4ee933aacb284e0d9b16576b910166bf1e01f58a46931fc0636a933c5.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{5x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(5x+2) & =3\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 5\\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =6\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =5x+2=5(2)+2=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot BC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =24\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252572 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fddca52e-d8ec-5acd-9f04-b74ff4127577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252574} {:answer/id #uuid "27248f76-3fcd-503e-8827-718b9ab3bd92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252575} {:answer/id #uuid "2a66f2ae-5e03-57b7-a978-dbdc33db814e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16.3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252576} {:answer/id #uuid "969e0922-6fdc-522d-8dcd-0e7cbf944a51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "13.4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252577} {:answer/id #uuid "bfc3f6a0-4ad8-531b-a05a-d49e1e9d895e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15.6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fddca52e-d8ec-5acd-9f04-b74ff4127577" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "14.5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252574} :answer-field/id #uuid "2bfeb9d4-a048-5bc6-a337-af552ccd8e41" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252573}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3fa83370-246b-52a5-bb67-0622bfb629ec" :question/math-academy-id "q-124471" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/f0d4e8ddf3a1b6cacab75f3207575695de5790f8223e30bc948e93daf37c939f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to one decimal place, find the area of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x-1}{x+2} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})(x+2) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =x-1 \\\\ x\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})-x & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x(\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})-1) & =-1-2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x(1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})) & =1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ x & =\\frac{1+2\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})}{1-\\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘})} \\\\ x & =5.098\\,0…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x-1=5.098\\,0-1=4.098\\,0…, \\\\ AB & =x+2=5.098\\,0+2=7.098\\,0….\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}(4.098\\,0…)(7.098\\,0…) \\\\  & =14.543\\,8… \\\\  & ≈14.5,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the one decimal place."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252579 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "703fe4a2-8381-563d-a086-8d740b5e8f9a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252581} {:answer/id #uuid "73fcb0dc-f733-515b-9bdd-bd69d99c2aff" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252582} {:answer/id #uuid "1a730108-7698-514a-a07e-3658f58d2c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252583} {:answer/id #uuid "72905faa-6ec6-5e72-aad8-deab943eb39b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252584} {:answer/id #uuid "8cf19cab-2d36-541e-b1e1-86d4871acc5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252585}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1a730108-7698-514a-a07e-3658f58d2c20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252583} :answer-field/id #uuid "4c495a22-3a33-5b67-929e-2652b984c5bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252580}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "963a40ef-ec42-5f96-ad58-c048d492c81f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124475" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/0ad5279a7ec9ac20a2c4e1449f93ae67854caf021aba8435165b80069f23afbd.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot AB.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠B={60}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{AC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+2} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+2) & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+2\\sqrt{3} & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3} & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =2\\sqrt{3}\\,x=2\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 2=4\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+2=2+2=4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AC\\cdot AB \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\sqrt{3}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252586 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "18617fe8-c9c0-5389-9dc8-ba1d26fe3faf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252588} {:answer/id #uuid "8ef00204-96ac-50b7-860a-ee6c79b1e81c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252589}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8ef00204-96ac-50b7-860a-ee6c79b1e81c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252589} :answer-field/id #uuid "829ca167-5326-547a-b735-659495b6b1de" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252587}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3d2f81dd-67ab-5130-8a01-588c2d7dd1e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-251064" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/fbccea4652fde939777bd69f621497f9e63ee79c7d4e4f0a5327bb141ce021ca.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of a right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =\\frac{6}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘}) & =6 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{6}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({70}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =2.183…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot (2.183…) \\\\  & =6.551… \\\\  & ≈7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252590 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ec7c2c13-0647-5bdf-9602-8d0941c1ae83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252592} {:answer/id #uuid "522ef804-a625-59cc-b29a-59baf4ed2e78" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "27" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252593}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec7c2c13-0647-5bdf-9602-8d0941c1ae83" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "26" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252592} :answer-field/id #uuid "61e9bf01-0d9f-50b1-a4c2-8d1af4dc9f92" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252591}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "aadee610-8257-53c0-bdd3-cdaae7e5f633" :question/math-academy-id "q-251069" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/85344df61b503271cd23cb3c741cd659b1417cb34b9031f0283dcf9c8fae6794.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{12} \\\\ AC & =12\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({20}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =4.367…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (4.367…)\\cdot 12 \\\\  & =26.205… \\\\  & ≈26,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7c85af72-d294-53bf-ad87-6c3f84ddb768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252596}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7c85af72-d294-53bf-ad87-6c3f84ddb768" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252596} :answer-field/id #uuid "db52aa00-509b-5012-a2fb-50707ea4aa2d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252595}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a687ddb-5483-5cff-9ddf-a1874dbba356" :question/math-academy-id "q-251070" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ed3de6f6fe96fab30d6f3927582a00ee9d0edc1f2514fec17507e2398009217f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{5} \\\\ AC & =5\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =2.886…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (2.886…)\\cdot 5 \\\\  & =7.216… \\\\  & ≈7,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252597 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a71591b4-86fd-5e2f-9882-8d1a20f2c845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252599}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a71591b4-86fd-5e2f-9882-8d1a20f2c845" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "52" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252599} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ded80de-2cbd-5d3c-a8a1-0bcda5e04703" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252598}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "117cc85c-6094-519a-9785-f355ef4c8616" :question/math-academy-id "q-251074" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/e72091463bf8f973629ff1467ae8ca184689b4745c387acac618b8a81876c52f.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, the area of $△ABC$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and need to determine the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) & =\\frac{AC}{14} \\\\ AC & =14\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({28}^{∘}) \\\\ AC & =7.443…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot (7.443…)\\cdot 14 \\\\  & =52.107… \\\\  & ≈52,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252600 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio of One Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1c4f597d-80b6-54bb-b310-968ef151ea20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252602}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c4f597d-80b6-54bb-b310-968ef151ea20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252602} :answer-field/id #uuid "5002344a-229b-5afb-8703-6daff5817d3a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252601}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f18363ef-03d9-5502-922b-35e61fbd60b0" :question/math-academy-id "q-251078" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/7acf00fc8ac1ac67612b740450fe62f7cddee2a9fc7a9c28fe54fafb2c1ee57c.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{5}{2},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{5}{2}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{5}{2} & =\\frac{3x-1}{12-5x} \\\\ 5(12-5x) & =2(3x-1) \\\\ 60-25x & =6x-2 \\\\ 31x & =62 \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =12-5x=12-5(2)=2, \\\\ AC & =3x-1=3(2)-1=5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252603 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio of One Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1297785f-656c-5acc-9e1b-5dc1c3f4ba2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252605}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1297785f-656c-5acc-9e1b-5dc1c3f4ba2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252605} :answer-field/id #uuid "2b1d34d4-3efb-5490-a42e-fc7d33a1f42e" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252604}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "89d89b73-504a-5f33-91c3-a6a449c6798e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251086" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/51e60c645aa6be034a8ef23d16a9ca7a815ca15fe815d7c3b03a866e693f3e5b.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=\\frac{2}{3}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ \\frac{2}{3} & =\\frac{10x-1}{8x+2} \\\\ 2(8x+2) & =3(10x-1) \\\\ 16x+4 & =30x-3 \\\\ 14x & =7 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =10x-1=10(\\frac{1}{2})-1=4, \\\\ AC & =8x+2=8(\\frac{1}{2})+2=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 4\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =12.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252606 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio of One Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86491e84-7a31-5e30-990e-33a0e59a7d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252608}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86491e84-7a31-5e30-990e-33a0e59a7d7a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252608} :answer-field/id #uuid "130001a8-a8c5-56f9-81ea-43f1bd107e68" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252607}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "213eedb1-565d-5f76-b007-4e78dbc869a4" :question/math-academy-id "q-251087" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/05003be9090f98f39a65d9ec33e8568fa43ec5c427e34398e4932708f8a03ccc.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=4.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 4 & =\\frac{11x-12}{x+4} \\\\ 4(x+4) & =11x-12 \\\\ 4x+16 & =11x-12 \\\\ 7x & =28 \\\\ x & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =11x-12=11(4)-12=32, \\\\ AC & =x+4=4+4=8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 32\\cdot 8 \\\\  & =128.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252609 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio of One Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "600b45b3-9266-5373-85b7-d2067f0f81ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252611} {:answer/id #uuid "4e44e423-5df9-50ca-b8ea-ec0d624532cf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "600b45b3-9266-5373-85b7-d2067f0f81ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252611} :answer-field/id #uuid "ed72c7f2-e36a-56d1-b136-fae8c66f4f9c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252610}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "c972b721-661a-53b1-be3e-5e738f66bd5d" :question/math-academy-id "q-251089" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/251ca3005dd302ec1e7ba0c7d7c497e28fd4c16cc0e431cc3691bdd4fe65446a.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B)=\\frac{1}{5}.$ Notice that relative to $∠B,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\frac{1}{5} & =\\frac{6x-1}{15x} \\\\ 15x & =5(6x-1) \\\\ 15x & =30x-5 \\\\ 15x & =5 \\\\ x & =\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =15x=15(\\frac{1}{3})=5, \\\\ AC & =6x-1=6(\\frac{1}{3})-1=1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 5\\cdot 1 \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252613 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given a Trigonometric Ratio of an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0c086cd4-1d45-5818-901a-8e06b11d2b37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "450" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252615} {:answer/id #uuid "3a5fa6d7-3d77-55f1-aa75-b9f548fa982c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "225" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252616}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3a5fa6d7-3d77-55f1-aa75-b9f548fa982c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "225" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252616} :answer-field/id #uuid "3e504436-4023-5f4b-99f4-15f12e0a9269" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252614}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "6e4f2531-54a0-5be4-a41b-03ab9dce1975" :question/math-academy-id "q-251121" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/214774fb428c62ad5131760c2a073690bca63f6b8bb06131c4381fee943597c3.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta =2,$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ adjacent to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to find the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{BC}{15} \\\\ BC & =2\\cdot 15 \\\\ BC & =30\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 30\\cdot 15 \\\\  & =225.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252617 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given a Trigonometric Ratio of an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c98fc282-138a-506a-8540-d4695139aef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c98fc282-138a-506a-8540-d4695139aef2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252619} :answer-field/id #uuid "72938f94-b6fb-512e-adeb-21228d24c46d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252618}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3a1be4ef-1b5d-5162-b0ca-0628ac21678e" :question/math-academy-id "q-251126" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ef2b0447e81370a50ea6d4115fc6f4687aff74fee17bc66f116b3c732667857e.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta =\\frac{2}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠B.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ adjacent to $∠B.$ Hence, we can use the cosine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{2}{7} & =\\frac{4}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{4}{2}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =14\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{14}^{2}-{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{196-16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{180} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\sqrt{5}\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =12\\sqrt{5}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252620 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given a Trigonometric Ratio of an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "cb248702-f541-551e-a9bf-d40ac94171d0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252622} {:answer/id #uuid "0c34f093-88d1-5c79-bea4-5cc38aeabc99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252623}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0c34f093-88d1-5c79-bea4-5cc38aeabc99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252623} :answer-field/id #uuid "f41d44f4-bb54-5588-9a0b-9481c1ca932b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252621}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e75dd5d8-326f-57e3-93b1-3e0bc2ea6f68" :question/math-academy-id "q-251130" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/6b1c6c90b25fa7c4cd4cde42bdcd5e69a2ccef63f1945067a8f62dc7ee779f05.png)\n\nGiven that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ the **exact** area of $△ABC$ shown above is{{field-1}} square units." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{7} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{AB} \\\\ AB & =\\frac{\\sqrt{13}}{\\sqrt{13}}\\cdot 7 \\\\ AB & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{7}^{2}-(\\sqrt{13})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49-13} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36} \\\\  & =6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{13}\\cdot 6 \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115594 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "437a71fe-92e0-58e3-9f49-6560b2755776" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given a Trigonometric Ratio of an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81fc652a-7b2e-5e4a-bb19-34d97e267d54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "64" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112965} {:answer/id #uuid "c28e0fb5-4670-5e52-9ae2-450d3a466cd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112966} {:answer/id #uuid "c3ee358c-5b7c-5d72-aa41-732ac755dfa8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112967} {:answer/id #uuid "ec89c962-70eb-5412-821e-5ea2810632d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112968} {:answer/id #uuid "3724b346-77c6-50d5-99b4-57984a07eab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112969}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ec89c962-70eb-5412-821e-5ea2810632d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "32\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112968} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cf81eb9-84ef-5c58-aad1-0caf0bab5fc4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112964}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "fe383b7e-4b92-5b53-b9c3-d588227c5371" :question/math-academy-id "q-28265" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/q-28265.png)\n\nGiven that $\\sin θ = \\frac{1}{2}$, calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta =\\frac{1}{2},$ where $\\theta =m∠A.$ Notice we're also given the length of the side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ opposite to $∠A.$ Hence, we can use the sine ratio to find the length of the hypotenuse $\\overset{―}{AB}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2} & =\\frac{8}{AB} \\\\ AB & =8(2) \\\\ AB & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can use the Pythagorean Theorem to find the missing side $AC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AC & =\\sqrt{A{B}^{2}-B{C}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{16}^{2}-{8}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{256-64} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{192} \\\\  & =8\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}BC\\cdot AC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 8\\cdot (8\\sqrt{3}) \\\\  & =32\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115595 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "51739685-2d53-5c9b-870b-b557ffdf2768" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given a Trigonometric Ratio of One Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e9ff682-e6a3-5a1e-b09d-964aaf36badc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112971} {:answer/id #uuid "96c49518-4a7a-53ea-8629-db3a4c9be64f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "20" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112972} {:answer/id #uuid "a32c5bfc-50fc-5a03-9aa3-5df5fa1e368e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112973} {:answer/id #uuid "fd84e58d-4914-5ca0-a80d-d2f85492f631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112974} {:answer/id #uuid "3ce36751-9eb4-5207-99b6-5c7f349581b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112975}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e9ff682-e6a3-5a1e-b09d-964aaf36badc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112971} :answer-field/id #uuid "9d35dbef-9fbc-52c1-bcf9-0f525ec88cec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186112970}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f0a77aee-e012-5d50-a91c-7eccfeb5ef38" :question/math-academy-id "q-28266" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/MA/DATA/Lessons/1608/Source/Images/q-28266.png)\n\nGiven that $\\tan (m∠A) = 5$, calculate the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A)=5.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AC} \\\\ 5 & =\\frac{2x+4}{x-1} \\\\ 5(x-1) & =2x+4 \\\\ 5x-5 & =2x+4 \\\\ 3x & =9 \\\\ x & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =2x+4=2(3)+4=10, \\\\ AC & =x-1=3-1=2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 10 \\\\  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252624 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c4312362-9961-5bf7-9423-42f4c2f7a13c" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Area of a Triangle Given an Angle and the Length of a Leg"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "22b1cb37-20ee-52fb-8882-b8b4c2f5c200" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "241" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252626} {:answer/id #uuid "17984ca8-7d3a-5510-8343-726a4e82c6c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "238" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252627} {:answer/id #uuid "9a9cf4f4-033d-5e68-ae76-6a09fdcadad0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "236" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252628} {:answer/id #uuid "dc189ced-daed-5439-a00d-0cfca665c5bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "245" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252629} {:answer/id #uuid "8d9f080a-f9d3-56ac-a070-100df577f177" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "233" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252630}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "17984ca8-7d3a-5510-8343-726a4e82c6c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "238" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252627} :answer-field/id #uuid "46230c9e-658d-5100-bb7f-79917ee1b44e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252625}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "f806f6d9-b146-5a87-9874-1eb64a7a1553" :question/math-academy-id "q-28308" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/43e5ba6bff8a20c20f8be2b18d57ad07fc030477d589a2ba43da0f2cb3816587.png)\n\nIn square units rounded to the nearest integer, what is the area of $△ABC$ shown above?" :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AC\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nNotice that relative to the given angle $∠B,$ we have the length of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{AC}$ and need to determine the length of the adjacent side $\\overset{―}{BC}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $BC:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠B) & =\\frac{AC}{BC} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘}) & =\\frac{20}{BC} \\\\ BC\\cdot \\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘}) & =20 \\\\ BC & =\\frac{20}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡({40}^{∘})} \\\\ BC & =23.835…\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 20\\cdot (23.835…) \\\\  & =238.350… \\\\  & ≈238,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252631 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "748a0451-e2b6-5b99-8cdc-1231435460b7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252633} {:answer/id #uuid "0b01be37-6df9-5d3c-a931-4ca7bde9f76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252634} {:answer/id #uuid "4c8dc388-d96d-5441-8eac-e1515b0b6352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "24\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252635} {:answer/id #uuid "bb6ee902-b8c8-53e4-a0de-fd12179780f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252636} {:answer/id #uuid "d23f457d-d71d-5f2b-b70e-3e38bab85939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b01be37-6df9-5d3c-a931-4ca7bde9f76b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252634} :answer-field/id #uuid "38b0548b-65ba-5330-a819-cab72a3ac58a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252632}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "da752c15-1fa7-5b59-b50f-3601de203814" :question/math-academy-id "q-76773" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ca9c6640b6cb239ae19b195731d8f605adae8826f66e10b075f7b0ad4a60690f.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={30}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({30}^{∘}) & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+4} \\\\ \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{3}\\,x}{x+4} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(x+4) & =3\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ \\sqrt{3}\\,x+4\\sqrt{3} & =3\\sqrt{3}\\,x \\\\ -2\\sqrt{3}\\,x & =-4\\sqrt{3} \\\\ x & =\\frac{4\\sqrt{3}}{2\\sqrt{3}} \\\\ x & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x=\\sqrt{3}(2)=2\\sqrt{3}, \\\\ AB & =x+4=2+4=6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186252638 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "fe83dedc-3034-5e3a-b546-dd57c0ccc6e8" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Area of a Triangle by Solving for a Variable Given an Angle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "af187634-a302-5b48-8602-42eb66afceb0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252640} {:answer/id #uuid "657098f6-f4ad-5f2d-8a27-b485160682f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252641} {:answer/id #uuid "01800aae-2f4b-5c50-8f93-57a557e1c1bf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252642} {:answer/id #uuid "7bbc8320-f6d7-51f4-b226-cebb5d54794f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252643} {:answer/id #uuid "66da1f44-731a-5a09-a260-c29255faf8a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252644}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bbc8320-f6d7-51f4-b226-cebb5d54794f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252643} :answer-field/id #uuid "19e5c726-5f44-5c16-93a4-0a873dc2a2c7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252639}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1386b559-f9dd-57ac-becb-7fb77e0e7576" :question/math-academy-id "q-76775" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13946119/assets/ab0e485908d86147b50e80f4d45c7e9966ab3453eb3ea01f6050bf1f7d88e2c8.png)\n\nFind the area (in square units) of $△ABC$ shown above." :question/worked-solution "In this case, the area of the right triangle is\n\n$$\nA=\\frac{1}{2}AB\\cdot BC.\n$$\n\nWe are given that $m∠A={60}^{∘}.$ Notice that relative to $∠A,$ we have expressions for the lengths of the opposite side $\\overset{―}{BC}$ and adjacent side $\\overset{―}{AB}.$ Hence, we can use the tangent ratio to solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡(m∠A) & =\\frac{BC}{AB} \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡({60}^{∘}) & =\\frac{x+2}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3} & =\\frac{x+2}{\\sqrt{3}\\,x} \\\\ \\sqrt{3}(\\sqrt{3}\\,x) & =x+2 \\\\ 3x & =x+2 \\\\ 2x & =2 \\\\ x & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the side lengths are \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BC & =x+2=1+2=3, \\\\ AB & =\\sqrt{3}\\,x=\\sqrt{3}(1)=\\sqrt{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of $△ABC$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot AB\\cdot BC \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot \\sqrt{3}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
